{"id": "REF_006", "split": "test", "question": "For pressing-emergency procurement under the TBS directive, what must be documented, and when is Treasury Board ratification/approval needed?", "mode": "cross_mode", "question_type": "emergency", "source_family_needed": ["tbs_directive"], "expected_doc_prefixes": ["tbs_directive__pol-doc-eng-aspx__id-32692__70db5331eb"], "gold_relevant_doc_prefixes": ["tbs_directive__pol-doc-eng-aspx__id-32692__70db5331eb"], "gold_relevant_chunk_ids": [], "claim_evidence": [{"claim": "The emergency file/report should document emergency justification, contract type/value, and why solicitation was impractical or impermissible.", "evidence_doc_prefixes": ["tbs_directive__pol-doc-eng-aspx__id-32692__70db5331eb"]}, {"claim": "TB approval or ratification is required for emergency contracts above specified thresholds.", "evidence_doc_prefixes": ["tbs_directive__pol-doc-eng-aspx__id-32692__70db5331eb"]}], "required_claims": ["The emergency file/report should document emergency justification, contract type/value, and why solicitation was impractical or impermissible.", "TB approval or ratification is required for emergency contracts above specified thresholds."], "forbidden_claims": ["Emergency contracts never require TB follow-up documentation."], "reference_answer": "Emergency use must be justified and documented, including why normal solicitation was not feasible, what authority was used, and contract value/type details. For high-value emergency contracts, TB approval or ratification requirements apply and must be addressed promptly.", "expect_abstain": false, "noise_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-create-solicitation-tender-notices-advanced-contract-award-notice__6941c7b148"], "contradiction_doc_prefixes": []}
{"id": "REF_007", "split": "test", "question": "If Buy Canadian framework language and the TBS procurement directive appear to point to different precedence rules, can we make a universal precedence claim from these excerpts alone?", "mode": "cross_mode", "question_type": "conflict", "source_family_needed": ["buy_canadian_policy", "tbs_directive"], "expected_doc_prefixes": ["buy_canadian_policy__en-buy-canadian-policy__e9189922a5", "tbs_directive__pol-doc-eng-aspx__id-32692__70db5331eb"], "gold_relevant_doc_prefixes": ["buy_canadian_policy__en-buy-canadian-policy__e9189922a5", "tbs_directive__pol-doc-eng-aspx__id-32692__70db5331eb"], "gold_relevant_chunk_ids": [], "claim_evidence": [{"claim": "The answer should avoid universal precedence claims when excerpts do not fully resolve all contexts.", "evidence_doc_prefixes": ["buy_canadian_policy__en-buy-canadian-policy__e9189922a5", "tbs_directive__pol-doc-eng-aspx__id-32692__70db5331eb"]}], "required_claims": ["A universal precedence claim should not be made without fully resolving scope and conflict clauses.", "When ambiguity remains, document rationale and escalate for policy/legal confirmation."], "forbidden_claims": ["One instrument always overrides the other in every case."], "reference_answer": "From these excerpts alone, you should not assert a universal override rule for every scenario. The safer policy-faithful response is to document applicability and conflict analysis for the specific procurement and escalate unresolved precedence questions for policy/legal review.", "expect_abstain": true, "noise_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-create-solicitation-tender-notices-advanced-contract-award-notice__6941c7b148"], "contradiction_doc_prefixes": []}
{"id": "REF_008", "split": "test", "question": "For procurements under a supply arrangement, summarize how trade-agreement thresholds change obligations and when an NPP is required.", "mode": "rfsa", "question_type": "trade_thresholds", "source_family_needed": ["buyers_guide"], "expected_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-create-solicitation-choose-solicitation-method-request-supply-arrangement__f09e4fcb6e"], "gold_relevant_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-create-solicitation-choose-solicitation-method-request-supply-arrangement__f09e4fcb6e"], "gold_relevant_chunk_ids": [], "claim_evidence": [{"claim": "Below threshold, trade agreement obligations do not apply.", "evidence_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-create-solicitation-choose-solicitation-method-request-supply-arrangement__f09e4fcb6e"]}, {"claim": "At or above threshold, agreements apply and NPP publication is required where applicable.", "evidence_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-create-solicitation-choose-solicitation-method-request-supply-arrangement__f09e4fcb6e"]}], "required_claims": ["Below threshold, trade agreement obligations do not apply.", "At or above threshold, agreements apply and NPP publication is required where applicable."], "forbidden_claims": [], "reference_answer": "For SA solicitations, threshold is the trigger: below the applicable trade threshold, the agreement obligations do not apply; at or above threshold, they apply, and where required a Notice of Proposed Procurement must be posted.", "expect_abstain": false, "noise_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-create-solicitation-tender-notices-advanced-contract-award-notice__6941c7b148"], "contradiction_doc_prefixes": []}
{"id": "REF_009", "split": "test", "question": "Explain to a new buyer: what makes a standing-offer call-up binding versus how binding happens under a supply arrangement?", "mode": "cross_mode", "question_type": "process", "source_family_needed": ["buyers_guide"], "expected_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-plan-determine-procurement-strategy-choose-method-supply__902b2afcf8"], "gold_relevant_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-plan-determine-procurement-strategy-choose-method-supply__902b2afcf8"], "gold_relevant_chunk_ids": [], "claim_evidence": [{"claim": "A call-up against a standing offer is acceptance and forms a binding contract for that procurement.", "evidence_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-plan-determine-procurement-strategy-choose-method-supply__902b2afcf8"]}, {"claim": "Under supply arrangements, each resulting contract is separately binding; qualification itself is not a contract to buy.", "evidence_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-plan-determine-procurement-strategy-choose-method-supply__902b2afcf8"]}], "required_claims": ["A call-up against a standing offer is acceptance and forms a binding contract for that procurement.", "Under supply arrangements, each resulting contract is separately binding; qualification itself is not a contract to buy."], "forbidden_claims": [], "reference_answer": "Standing offer: the call-up is the acceptance and creates the binding contract. Supply arrangement: prequalification is not itself a purchase contract; each awarded contract under the arrangement is separately binding.", "expect_abstain": false, "noise_doc_prefixes": ["buyers_guide__en-buyer-s-portal-buyer-s-guide-create-solicitation-tender-notices-advanced-contract-award-notice__6941c7b148"], "contradiction_doc_prefixes": []}
